# Line endings.
#
# Every text file in this repository is stored with LF, and some of them are
# compared byte for byte at test time: the golden documents under
# internal/router/testdata are diffed against generator output, and the
# generators always write "\n".
#
# Git for Windows enables core.autocrlf by default, which rewrites text files to
# CRLF on checkout. That made every line of every golden file differ by a
# trailing \r, and TestGoldenSpecs failed on Windows for a reason that had
# nothing to do with the code -- 883 of 883 lines "different", each one visually
# identical to its counterpart.
#
# text=auto keeps Git's content detection, so binaries are still left alone;
# eol=lf pins the working-tree ending on every platform no matter what the
# developer's autocrlf is set to. Nothing in the repository is stored with CRLF
# today, so this normalises working trees without rewriting a single blob.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures that are compared byte for byte. Covered by the rule above, but
# spelled out so the requirement is discoverable from this file and survives
# anyone loosening the global default.
**/testdata/** text eol=lf
